> 50. **Focus origins are enumerated by grep, never sampled.** For any task where focus moves or the focused element can unmount, B runs one regex over the files the task grants plus, found by grep, the callers of every action that can remove the focused element (e.g. `undo\(\)|redo\(\)`), never a hand-picked list and never the whole folder (206 hits): `onPointerDown(Capture)?|onBlur|settleEditor\(|\.focus\(|^\s*\{[^}]*(\.map\(|&&|\?)`. The last alternative catches JSX list renders and conditional renders, including multi-line ternaries (the old `\{[^}]*&&\s*<` matched 0 lines, C-R245-03). B pastes the command and hit count into the task. Every hit gets an expected `document.activeElement` row or a written out-of-scope ruling; C re-runs the grep, and a hit with neither is a planning FAIL. Evidence: the grid-menu chain 241 FAIL → 242 → 243 → 244 found one new origin class per round; B-R243-UNDO-MARKER-FOCUS (retro-245 §3; `tech-lead`, `consequence-tester`) (4×); C-R245-03 (regex fix, 1×).
